# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored — never commit real values.
# Per-site deploy vars (site dir, Cloudflare deploy hook) are no longer set
# here — each instance's own adapter declares and reads them from that
# instance repo's own .env (e.g. theprojection-data/.env carries
# THEPROJECTION_SITE_DIR/THEPROJECTION_DEPLOY_HOOK). This file only holds
# engine-level collector keys.

# --- Required: declared contact -------------------------------------------
# Several sources (SEC EDGAR, Federal Register, GDELT, OpenAlex) require or
# request a contact address in the User-Agent under their fair-access or
# polite-pool policies. kestrel ships no default — supply your own. The
# affected collectors fail loudly rather than send a fabricated contact.
KESTREL_CONTACT_EMAIL=

# Optional override for OpenAlex's polite pool specifically; falls back to
# KESTREL_CONTACT_EMAIL when unset.
# OPENALEX_MAILTO=

# --- Tier-2 collector keys (candidates in sources/sources.yaml — uncomment
# and fill in as each source's collector is actually wired; none of these
# are consumed yet by collectors/google_news_rss.py, which needs no key) ---

# FRED (money lens — macro series). Signup: https://fred.stlouisfed.org/docs/api/api_key.html
# FRED_API_KEY=

# LegiScan (state/federal bill tracking). Signup: https://legiscan.com/legiscan
# LEGISCAN_KEY=

# Congress.gov API. Signup: https://api.congress.gov/sign-up/
# CONGRESS_GOV_KEY=

# Regulations.gov (uses an api.data.gov key). Signup: https://api.data.gov/signup/
# REGULATIONS_GOV_KEY=

# GovInfo (also an api.data.gov key). Signup: https://api.data.gov/signup/
# GOVINFO_KEY=

# Semantic Scholar. Signup: https://www.semanticscholar.org/product/api#api-key-form
# SEMANTIC_SCHOLAR_KEY=

# GitHub (repo/release watch). Create a token: https://github.com/settings/tokens
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# OpenAlex polite-pool contact email (not a key — a real mailto gets you the
# fast lane; mint a kestrel-specific address, don't reuse an old one — see
# REBUILD-NOTES.md). Docs: https://docs.openalex.org/how-to-use-the-api/rate-limits-and-authentication
# OPENALEX_MAILTO=
# --- pre-existing keys (BOOTSTRAP "Keys" item — Ben may already hold these) ---
# COURTLISTENER_TOKEN=      # https://www.courtlistener.com/profile/api-token/ (optional — bumps the 5/min anon quota)
# DATA_GOV_API_KEY=         # https://api.data.gov/signup/
# LDA_API_KEY=              # https://lda.senate.gov/api/register/
# OPENSECRETS_API_KEY — slot removed 2026-07-28: OpenSecrets discontinued
# their API in 2025. Money-in-politics replacement: FEC API
# (api.open.fec.gov) accepts DATA_GOV_API_KEY — no new slot needed.
